<!-- Batch D2 violations fixture: exactly one dedicated violator per rule; every
     other value-level construct is compliant so each rule fires exactly once.
       0055 - IT.SUPPAE.QVAL (Name="QVAL", no def:ValueListRef); IT.SUPPLB.QVAL is
              the compliant QVAL decoy
       0080 - def:WhereClauseRef without WhereClauseOID (VL.WCREF, first ItemRef)
       0081 - def:WhereClauseRef WhereClauseOID="WC.DANGLING" (VL.WCREF, second ItemRef)
       0082 - the OID-less def:WhereClauseDef (second WhereClauseDef, xpath index [2])
       0083 - WC.BADCOMMENT def:CommentOID="COM.MISSING"; WC.OK carries a resolvable
              def:CommentOID decoy
       0085 - WC.EMPTY (no RangeCheck child)
       0086 - WC.BADCOMP RangeCheck Comparator="EQUALS"
       0087 - WC.NOCOMP RangeCheck without Comparator
       0088 - WC.BADSH RangeCheck SoftHard="Firm"
       0089 - WC.NOSH RangeCheck without SoftHard
       0090 - WC.NOITEM RangeCheck without def:ItemOID
       0091 - WC.BADITEM RangeCheck def:ItemOID="IT.MISSING"
       0092 - WC.NOCV RangeCheck without CheckValue
       0162 - IT.VS.VSORRES with two def:ValueListRef children (both resolvable)
       0163 - IT.LB.LBORRES def:ValueListRef ValueListOID="VL.DANGLING"
       0164 - IT.EG.EGORRES def:ValueListRef without ValueListOID
       0235 - VL.TWODESC with two Description children
       0236 - the OID-less def:ValueListDef (has an ItemRef so 0237 stays silent)
       0237 - VL.NOITEMS (no ItemRef child) -->
